## Layout

```
{{project_name}}/
  {{project_name}}.lmproject  the manifest (JSON): name, levels, input actions, maps & modes, physics, packaging, plugins
  contents/                   every asset, one .lmas file each
    levels/ meshes/static/ meshes/skeletal/ materials/ textures/ animations/ audio/
    blueprints/ widgets/ input/ enums/ interfaces/ particles/ landscapes/
  lib/                        Dart generated from the assets (main.dart, levels/, actors/, widgets/) + your own code
  plugins/                    project plugins (source-level Dart packages, see the create-plugin skill)
  .lumina/                    editor data: editor/ (this project's editor host), trash/, plugins/<plugin>/
  Saved/SaveGames/            save slots written while playing in the editor
  DerivedDataCache/           rebuildable editor cache (gitignored)
  pubspec.yaml                the game's Flutter package (the engine is a dependency)
  {{claude_skills_dir}}/  {{antigravity_skills_dir}}/   the Lumina skills, one copy per agent tool
```

- An `.lmas` asset is the bytes `LMAS` followed by JSON (`asset_id`, `name`, `type`, `metadata`, `references`,
  base64 `raw_payload`). Asset paths are project-relative and `/`-separated: `contents/blueprints/BP_Door.lmas`.
- `lib/` is generated: saving a level writes `lib/main.dart` and `lib/levels/<level>.dart`, compiling a Blueprint
  writes `lib/actors/<name>.dart`, compiling a Widget Blueprint writes `lib/widgets/`. Only the marked user-code
  regions in `lib/actors/` survive the next generation.

